In the Cartesian coordinate system, vertex A of right triangle OAB is on the positive half of the x-axis. The coordinates of vertex B are (3, \sqrt{3}), point C has coordinates (\frac{1}{2}, 0), and point P is a moving point on hypotenuse OB. What is the minimum value of PA + PC?
A. \frac{\sqrt{13}}{2}
B. \frac{\sqrt{31}}{2}
C. \frac{3+\sqrt{19}}{2}
D. 2 \sqrt{7}

In the figure, sector OAB is the lateral surface development of a cone. If the side length of each small square grid is 1 cm, what is the radius of the base of this cone in centimeters?
A. \frac{1}{2}
B. \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}
C. \sqrt{2}
D. 2\sqrt{2}

As shown in the figure, if the rectangular paper is folded along the dashed line ① and then cut along the dashed line ② to cut out a right triangle, the unfolded shape will be an isosceles triangle. What is the perimeter of the triangle after unfolding?
A. 2 + \sqrt{10}
B. 2 + 2 \sqrt{10}
C. 12
D. 18

The image shows a simple combination of three views, where the front view and side view are composed of an equilateral triangle and a square, and the top view is a square with a diagonal. What is the volume of this simple geometric body?
A. 8+\begin{tabular}{c}4\\3\end{tabular}\begin{tabular}{cc}\\3\end{tabular}
B. 4+\begin{tabular}{c}8\\3\end{tabular}\begin{tabular}{cc}\\3\end{tabular}
C. \begin{tabular}{c}28\\3\end{tabular}
D. \begin{tabular}{c}32\\3\end{tabular}
